# Dolby DAX Codec2 store. Verbatim from the stock vendor_service_contexts:132,
# where it sits beside the QTI store at default2 that we already carry.
#
# This one was missed when the Dolby stack was labelled, and it is the exact
# failure shape described in the comment above: the VINTF fragment
# vendor.dolby.media.c2-default-service-dax.xml declares
# IComponentStore/default9, so clients call waitForService() on it, while
# servicemanager refuses the registration because the name has no label. The
# result is not a denial in the log — it is a client that blocks forever.
#
# hal_codec2_service is an AOSP type (system/sepolicy/public/service.te:315).
# The service has no seclabel of its own; it runs in the mediacodec domain via
# the mediacodec_exec label on its binary (file_contexts:39), matching stock.
#
# Note that mediacodec is not a hal_codec2_server in AOSP, so under enforcing
# it will additionally need permission to add this service. That rule is
# deliberately NOT guessed here: the first flash boots permissive, where the
# add is allowed and the denial is recorded, and a rule written against a real
# denial is narrower than one written against a prediction. The label, by
# contrast, cannot wait — Access.cpp:167-170 fails the selabel lookup before
# it ever consults enforcing mode.
android.hardware.media.c2.IComponentStore/default9              u:object_r:hal_codec2_service:s0
